<h1>Hey, I'm Marcel</h1>

<p>I've been building software for about 25 years. Long enough to be skeptical of most hype, and close enough to the current AI shift to know this one is different.</p>

<p>Most of my work now sits where product, engineering, and founder reality meet. I like small teams, useful systems, and tools that make people feel more capable instead of more impressed.</p>

<p>I'm building <a href="https://boldvideo.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bold Video</a>, a video intelligence platform for coaching programs with large libraries that should be helping students instead of gathering dust.</p>

<p>I also work on <a href="https://sprintzero.sh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SprintZero</a>, where we help SaaS teams modernize legacy codebases in focused 30-day sprints, and <a href="https://founderwell.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FounderWell</a>, Vanessa's support system for founders in the messy middle between idea and exit.</p>

<p>And I make <a href="https://pidro.online" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pidro</a>, a multiplayer card game with 70k players, because apparently I can't help myself.</p>

<p>Based in Denia, Spain with my <a href="https://utmb.world/runner/2428139.monika.fahle" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">wife</a> and two kids. We run a lot.</p>

<p>Nice to have you here.</p>

